  <Document>
    <name>The Negro Motorist Green Book: 1946</name>
    <description>Published in 1946 as the first post-World War II edition following the 1942-1945 wartime hiatus, introducing the motto &#x27;Carry your Green Book with you... you may need it&#x27; and expanding to 3,335 listings. Preserved in the Library of Congress collection.</description>
